## 1. Project Overview

NED-OS is a personal Linux customization and desktop productivity project focused on building a personalized, efficient, visually consistent, and developer-friendly Linux environment.

The project initially started on Linux Mint and later transitioned to Fedora Linux. What began as a desktop customization experiment gradually evolved into a broader project involving terminal customization, system information dashboards, automation scripts, shell enhancements, custom utilities, and desktop integration.

NED-OS aims to provide a unified environment with custom branding, developer-oriented tools, and convenient system management features.

## 2. Development History

### Phase 1: Linux Mint Development

- Started developing NED-OS using Linux Mint.
- Customized desktop themes, icons, wallpapers, and panels.
- Experimented with desktop widgets and dock customization.
- Developed scripts for common Linux operations.
- Explored different desktop layouts and visual styles.
- Established the NED-OS branding and project structure.

### Phase 2: Migration to Fedora

- Migrated the primary development environment from Linux Mint to Fedora Linux.
- Adapted NED-OS configurations for Fedora.
